(5) In-depth studying the photocatalytic mechanisms. Although MOFs have been widely used in the field of heterogeneous photocatalysis, their detailed photocatalytic mechanisms are far from clear. The differences of active sites on surface or within the pores for catalytic reactions are also unclear. Considering the reactive species only exist for a fleeting moment, advanced characterization and theoretical calculation would be necessary for probing the catalytic cycles. A better understanding of ROS generation and reaction mechanism can be fed back to the further design and synthesis of photocatalytic MOF materials.
Overall, the huge research prospects and application potential of MOF photocatalysts are self-evident, but continuous studies are still needed to explore MOF photocatalysts for further improved charge separation and transfer. Other than that, the structural robustness of MOF photocatalysts is equally important in order to survive harsh reaction conditions and meet the industrial application requirements. We hope that this review can help researchers to better understand the current state of MOF photocatalysis and find breakthroughs for further development and application of MOF photocatalysts.
